A [_] arm without a lacuna, on a field beneath a struct: the lacuna the help
offers nests the field in its struct, as lacunas are written.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		kind: string
	}
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		kind: int
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		meta: {
			kind: _match(v0_0.meta.kind, {
				"a": 1
				[_]: 0
			})
		}
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		kind: int
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0414]: the [_] arm collapses every unmatched value into one, and no lacuna says what is lost
  --> history/1.0.thema:13:5
   |
13 |                 [_]: 0
   |                 ^
   |
   = help: declare what is lost in lacunas: {meta: {kind: [{type: Type, message: "..."}]}}
